<title>SRI LANKA: Hilton to manage JAIC Sri Lanka apartment complex.</title>
<headline>Hilton to manage JAIC Sri Lanka apartment complex.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hotels group Hilton International said on Tuesday it had signed an agreement to manage a 34-storey, $80 million residential apartment complex in Colombo, Sri Lanka, with Japan Asia Investment Co Ltd (JAIC).</p>
<p>Hilton said in a statement the deal was signed between Teiji Imahara, chairman of JAIC and Alain Mahillon, vice president, Hilton International, Southeast Asia.</p>
<p>The building comprises 175 fully furnished 2- and 3-bedroom apartments and eight luxury penthouses.</p>
<p>-- Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
